{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-1","title":"Ezekiel 20:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 God refuses to be consulted by the elders of Israel. 4 He shews the story of their rebellions in Egypt, 10 in the wilderness, 27 and in the land. 33 He promises to gather them by the Gospel. 45 Under the name of a forest he shews the destruction of Jerusalem.</p>\n<p>A.M. 3411. B.C. 593. in the seventh.The seventh year of the captivity of Jeconiah, and according to Usher, Monday, Aug. 27, 3411.</p>\n<p>1:2; 8:1; 24:1; 26:1; 29:1,17; 30:20; 31:1; 32:1; 40:1 that certain. 14:1-3; 33:30-33; 1Ki 14:2-6; 22:15-28; 2Ki 3:13; Isa 29:13; 58:2 Jer 37:17; Mt 22:16 and sat. 8:1; Lu 2:46; 8:35; 10:39; Ac 22:3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-3","title":"Ezekiel 20:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>Are. Isa 1:12; Mt 3:7; Lu 3:7 As I. 31; 14:3,4,7,8; 1Sa 28:6; Ps 50:15-21; Pr 15:8; 21:27; 28:9 Isa 1:15; Mic 3:7; Mt 15:8,9; Joh 4:24</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-4","title":"Ezekiel 20:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>judge them. or, plead for them. 14:14,20; 22:2; 23:36,45; Isa 5:3; Jer 7:16; 11:14; 14:11-14; 15:1 1Co 6:2 cause. 16:2,3; Mt 23:29-37; Lu 11:47-51; 13:33-35; Ac 7:51,52</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-5","title":"Ezekiel 20:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>In the. Ex 6:6,7; 19:4-6; De 4:37; 7:6; 14:2; Ps 33:12; Isa 41:8,9; 43:10 Isa 44:1,2; Jer 33:24; Mr 13:20 lifted up mine hand. or, sware. (and so ver. 6, etc.Ex 6:8, 9.) 15,23; 47:14; Ge 14:22; De 32:40; Re 10:5 and made. 35:11; Ex 3:8; 4:31; De 4:34; 11:2-7; Ps 103:7 I am. Ex 3:6,16; 20:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-6","title":"Ezekiel 20:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>lifted. 5,15,23,42 to bring. Ge 15:13,14; Ex 3:8,17; 14:1-15:27 into. De 8:7-9; 11:11,12; 32:8 flowing. Ex 13:5; 33:3; Le 20:24; Nu 13:27; 14:8; De 6:3; 11:9; 26:9,15; 27:3 De 31:20; 32:13,14; Jos 5:6; Jer 11:5; 32:22 which is. 15; Ps 48:2; Da 8:9; 11:16,41; Zec 7:14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-7","title":"Ezekiel 20:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>Cast. 8; 18:6,15,31; Isa 2:20,21; 31:7 the abominations. 6:9; 14:6; 2Ch 15:8 defile. 23:3,8; Le 17:7; 18:3; De 29:16-18; Jos 24:14 I am. 19; Ex 16:12; Le 11:44; 20:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-8","title":"Ezekiel 20:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>they rebelled. De 9:7; Ne 9:26; Isa 63:10 they did. 7; Ex 32:4-6 then I. 13,21; 5:13; 7:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-9","title":"Ezekiel 20:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>I wrought. 14,22; 36:21,22; 39:7; Ex 32:12; Nu 14:13-25; De 9:28; 32:26,27 Jos 7:9; 1Sa 12:22 in whose. Jos 2:10; 9:9,10; 1Sa 4:8</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-10","title":"Ezekiel 20:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>Ex 13:17,18; 14:17-22; 15:22; 20:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-11","title":"Ezekiel 20:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>I gave. De 4:8; Ne 9:13,14; Ps 147:19,20; Ro 3:2 shewed them. Heb. made them to know. which. 13,21; Le 18:5; De 20:15,16; Lu 10:28; Ro 10:5; Ga 3:12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-12","title":"Ezekiel 20:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>I gave. Ge 2:3; Ex 16:29; 20:8-11; 35:2; Le 23:3,24,32,39; 25:4; De 5:12-15 Ne 9:14; Mr 2:27,28; Col 2:16 to be. 20; Ex 31:13-17 I am. 37:28; Ex 19:5,6; Le 20:8; 21:8,15,23; Joh 17:17-19; 1Th 5:23 Jude 1:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-13","title":"Ezekiel 20:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>rebelled. 8; Ex 16:28; 32:8; Nu 14:22; De 9:12-24; 31:27; 1Sa 8:8 Ne 9:16-18; Ps 78:40,41; 95:8-11; 106:13-33; Isa 63:10 and they. 16,24; Le 26:15,43; 2Sa 12:9; Pr 1:25; 13:13; Am 2:4; 1Th 4:8 Heb 10:28,29 which. 11 and my. 21; Ex 16:27,28; Nu 15:31-36; Isa 56:6 I said. 8,21; Ex 32:10; Nu 14:11,12,29; 16:20,21,45; 26:25; De 9:8 Ps 106:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-14","title":"Ezekiel 20:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>9,22; 36:22,23; Eph 1:6,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-15","title":"Ezekiel 20:15","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":15,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":15},"content":"<p>I lifted. 23; Nu 14:23-30; 26:64,65; De 1:34,35; Ps 95:11; 106:26; Heb 3:11 Heb 3:18; 4:3 flowing. 6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-16","title":"Ezekiel 20:16","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":16,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":16},"content":"<p>they. 13,14 for their.They still had a hankering after the idolatries they had learned in Egypt, to which they added new idols, which they had seen in countries through which they had travelled, as those of the Midianites, Amorites, etc.</p>\n<p>8; 14:3,4; 23:8; Ex 32:1-8; Nu 15:39; 25:2; Am 5:25,26; Ac 7:39-43</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-17","title":"Ezekiel 20:17","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":17,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":17},"content":"<p>mine. 8:18; 9:10; 1Sa 24:10; Ne 9:19; Ps 78:37,38 neither. 7:2; 11:13; Jer 4:27; 5:18; Na 1:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-18","title":"Ezekiel 20:18","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":18,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":18},"content":"<p>I said. Nu 14:32,33; 32:13-15; De 4:3-6; Ps 78:6-8 the statutes. Zec 1:2-4; Lu 11:47,48; Ac 7:51; 1Pe 1:18 defile. 7; Jer 2:7; 3:9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-19","title":"Ezekiel 20:19","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":19,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":19},"content":"<p>the Lord. Ex 20:2,3; De 5:6,7; 7:4-6; Ps 81:9,10; Jer 3:22,23 walk. 11:20; 36:27; 37:24; De 4:1; 5:1,32,33; 6:1-8:20; 10:1-12:32 Ne 9:13,14; Ps 19:7-11; 105:45; Tit 2:11-14</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-20","title":"Ezekiel 20:20","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":20,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":20},"content":"<p>12; 44:24; Ex 20:11; 31:13-17; Ne 13:15-22; Isa 58:13 Jer 17:22,24,27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-21","title":"Ezekiel 20:21","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":21,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":21},"content":"<p>the children. Nu 21:5; 25:1-8; De 9:23,24; 31:27; Ps 106:29-33; Ac 13:18 if a man. 11,13 I would. 8,13; 21:31; 2Ch 34:21,25; Re 16:1 accomplish. 7:8; 13:15; La 4:11; Da 11:36</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-22","title":"Ezekiel 20:22","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":22,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":22},"content":"<p>I withdrew. 17; Job 13:21; Ps 78:38; La 2:8 wrought. 9,14,22; Ps 25:11; 79:9,10; 115:1; Isa 48:9-11; Jer 14:7,21 Da 9:17,19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-23","title":"Ezekiel 20:23","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":23,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":23},"content":"<p>lifted. 15; De 32:40; Re 10:5,6 that I.The predictions of the dispersion of Israel, delivered by Moses just before his death, are evidently here referred to: they received a partial accomplishment at the Babylonian captivity, but are more exactly fulfilling at this day.</p>\n<p>Le 26:33; De 28:64-68; 32:26,27; Ps 106:27; Jer 15:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-24","title":"Ezekiel 20:24","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":24,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":24},"content":"<p>they had. 13,16 their eyes. 6:9; 18:6,12,15; De 4:19; Job 31:26,27; Am 2:4</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-25","title":"Ezekiel 20:25","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":25,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":25},"content":"<p>I gave.The simple meaning of this place is, that when the Israelites had rebelled against God, despised his statutes, and polluted his sabbaths, in effect cast him off, and given themselves up wholly to their idols, then He, in a just judgment for their disobedience, abandoned them, \"gave them up to a reprobate mind,\" (Ro 1:28,) and suffered them to walk after the idolatrous, cruel, and impious customs and ordinances of the heathen; by which they were ripened for the destruction which he intended to bring upon them, that they might learn to know God by his judgments, seeing they had despised his mercies. In the same sense God is said judicially to \"send a strong delusion, that they should believe a lie,\" to those who \"received not the love of the truth, but had pleasure in unrighteousness.\"</p>\n<p>26,39; 14:9-11; De 4:27,28; 28:36; Ps 81:12; Isa 66:4; Ro 1:21-28 2Th 2:9-11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-26","title":"Ezekiel 20:26","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":26,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":26},"content":"<p>polluted. 31; Isa 63:17; Ro 11:7-10 in that. 16:20,21; Le 18:21; 2Ki 17:17; 21:6; 2Ch 28:3; 33:6; Jer 32:35 all that. Ex 13:12; Lu 2:23 to the end. 6:7</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-27","title":"Ezekiel 20:27","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":27,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":27},"content":"<p>speak. 2:7; 3:4,11,27 Yet. Ro 2:24; Re 13:5 committed. Heb. trespassed.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-28","title":"Ezekiel 20:28","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":28,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":28},"content":"<p>when I. Jos 23:3,4,14; Ne 9:22-26; Ps 78:55-58 the which. 6,15; Ge 15:18-21; 26:3,4; Ps 105:8-11 they saw. 6:13; Ps 78:58; Isa 57:5-7; Jer 2:7; 3:6 their sweet. 16:19</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-29","title":"Ezekiel 20:29","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":29,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":29},"content":"<p>I said, etc. or, I told them what the high place was, or,Bamah. And the. 16:24,25,31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-30","title":"Ezekiel 20:30","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":30,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":30},"content":"<p>Are ye. Nu 32:14; Jud 2:19; Jer 7:26; 9:14; 16:12; Mt 23:32; Ac 7:51</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-31","title":"Ezekiel 20:31","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":31,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":31},"content":"<p>ye offer. 26; De 18:10-12; Ps 106:37-39; Jer 7:31; 19:5 and shall. 3; 14:3,4; 1Sa 28:5,6; 2Ki 3:13,14; Job 27:8,10; Ps 66:18 Pr 1:27,28; 28:9; Isa 1:15; Jer 14:12; Zec 7:13; Mt 25:11,12 Jas 4:1-3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-32","title":"Ezekiel 20:32","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":32,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":32},"content":"<p>that which. 11:5; 38:10; Ps 139:2; Pr 19:21; La 3:37 We will. 1Sa 8:5; Jer 44:17,29; Ro 12:2 to serve. De 4:28; 28:36,64; 29:17; Isa 37:19; Da 5:4; Re 9:20</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-33","title":"Ezekiel 20:33","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":33,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":33},"content":"<p>surely. 8:18; Jer 21:5; 42:18; 44:6; La 2:4; Da 9:11,12</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-34","title":"Ezekiel 20:34","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":34,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":34},"content":"<p>38; 34:16; Isa 27:9-13; Am 9:9,10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-35","title":"Ezekiel 20:35","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":35,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":35},"content":"<p>I will. 36; 19:13; 38:8; Ho 2:14; Mic 4:10; 7:13-15; Re 12:14 and there. 17:20; 38:22; Jer 2:9,35; 25:31; Ho 4:1; Mic 6:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-36","title":"Ezekiel 20:36","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":36,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":36},"content":"<p>13,21; Ex 32:7-35; Nu 11:1-35; 14:1-45; 16:1-50; 25:1-18 Ps 106:15-48; 1Co 10:5-10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-37","title":"Ezekiel 20:37","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":37,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":37},"content":"<p>pass. 34:17; Le 27:32; Jer 33:13; Mt 25:32,33 I will. 16:59,60; Le 26:25; Ps 89:30-32; Am 3:2 the bond. or, a delivering.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-38","title":"Ezekiel 20:38","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":38,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":38},"content":"<p>I will purge. 11:21; 34:17,20-22; Nu 14:28-30; Am 9:9,10; Zec 13:8,9; Mal 3:3 Mal 4:1-3; Mt 3:9,10,12; 25:32,33; Ro 9:27-29 they shall. 13:9; Nu 14:30; Ps 95:11; Jer 44:14; 1Co 10:5; Heb 4:6; Jude 1:5 and ye. 6:7; 15:7; 23:49; Ps 9:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-39","title":"Ezekiel 20:39","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":39,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":39},"content":"<p>Go ye. 25,26; Jud 10:14; 2Ki 3:13; Ps 81:12; Ho 4:17; Am 4:4,5 Ro 1:24-28; 2Th 2:11 but. 23:37-39; Pr 21:27; Isa 1:13-15; 66:3; Jer 7:9-11; Zep 1:4,5 Mt 6:24; Re 3:15,16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-40","title":"Ezekiel 20:40","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":40,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":40},"content":"<p>in mine.These predictions received a partial accomplishment by the restoration of the Jews from the Babylonian captivity; but they seem chiefly to relate to the establishment of the Christian church, and more especially to the future conversion of the Jews, and their restoration to their own land.</p>\n<p>17:23; Ps 2:6; 68:15,16; Isa 2:2,3; 66:20; Jer 31:12; Joe 3:17,18 Ob 1:16; Mic 4:1,2; Heb 12:20-22; Re 21:10 there shall. 37:22-28; Isa 56:7; 60:7; 66:23; Zec 8:20-23; Mal 1:11; 3:4; Re 12:1 Heb 13:15; 1Pe 2:5 first-fruits. or, chief.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-41","title":"Ezekiel 20:41","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":41,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":41},"content":"<p>with your. 28; 6:13; Ge 8:21; Le 1:9,13,17; Eph 5:2; Php 4:18 sweet savour. Heb. savour of rest. I bring. 11:17; 34:19; 36:24; 37:25; 38:8; Isa 11:11-16; 27:12,13; Jer 23:3 Jer 30:3,18; 32:37; Am 9:14; Ob 1:17-21; Mic 7:12-16 and I will. 28:22,25; 38:23; 39:27-29; Le 10:3; Isa 5:16; Lu 2:14; 1Pe 3:15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-42","title":"Ezekiel 20:42","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":42,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":42},"content":"<p>ye shall. 38,44; 24:24; 26:13; 36:23; 38:23; Jer 24:7; 31:34; Joh 17:3 1Jo 5:20 when I. 11:17-20; 34:13; 36:24; 37:21,25 for the which. 15</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-43","title":"Ezekiel 20:43","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":43,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":43},"content":"<p>shall ye. 6:9; Le 26:39-41; Ne 1:8-10; Ho 5:15 and ye shall. 16:61-63; 36:31; Job 42:6; Jer 31:18; Zec 12:10-14; Lu 18:13 2Co 7:11</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-44","title":"Ezekiel 20:44","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":44,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":44},"content":"<p>And ye shall. 38; 24:24 when I. 9,14,22; 36:21,22; Ps 79:9; 115:1; Eph 1:6; 1Ti 1:16</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-45","title":"Ezekiel 20:45","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":45,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":45},"content":"<p>Moreover.This is the beginning of another prophecy, and properly belongs to the following chapter.</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-46","title":"Ezekiel 20:46","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":46,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":46},"content":"<p>set. 4:7; 6:2 toward.Towards Judea, which lay south of Mesopotamia, where the prophet now dwelt.</p>\n<p>and drop. 21:2; De 32:2; Job 29:22; Am 7:16; Mic 2:6; *marg: the forest.The city of Jerusalem, as full of inhabitants as the forest is of trees.</p>\n<p>Jer 13:19; 22:7; Zec 11:1,2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-47","title":"Ezekiel 20:47","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":47,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":47},"content":"<p>I will kindle.I will send war; and it shall destroy all ranks and characters of the people.</p>\n<p>15:6,7; 19:14; 22:20,21; De 32:22; Isa 9:18,19; 30:33; Jer 21:14 green. 17:24; Lu 23:31 the flaming. Isa 66:24; Mr 9:43-49 from the south. 21:3,4; Isa 24:1-6</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-48","title":"Ezekiel 20:48","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":48,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":48},"content":"<p>De 29:24-28; 2Ch 7:20-22; Isa 26:11; Jer 40:2,3; La 2:16,17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-ezk-20-49","title":"Ezekiel 20:49","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"EZK","chapterStart":20,"verseStart":49,"chapterEnd":20,"verseEnd":49},"content":"<p>Doth.Is it not his usual custom to deal in enigmas? His figures are not to be understood; we should not trouble ourselves with them. God therefore commands the prophet to declare, in the next chapter, the same things in the plainest terms, so that they should not complain of his parables.</p>\n<p>Mt 13:13,14; Joh 16:25; Ac 17:18</p>"}]}